# What never enters the image build context.
#
# Two jobs, and the first one matters far more than image size: nothing here that holds a
# secret may ever be baked into a layer. A config.yaml copied into an image carries the
# provider credentials and notification webhook tokens of whoever built it, and layers are
# readable by anyone who pulls the image.
#
# Guarded by tests/test_docker_packaging.py - add a secret-bearing path here and there too.

# --- Secrets and live state (the leak guard) ---
config.yaml
config.local.yaml
instance/
dvr.db
dvr.db-shm
dvr.db-wal
dvr.db-journal
capture-logs/
*.log
dvr.log.*
# Support bundles download into the repo root and hold account and channel names, dvr.log and
# the (masked) config. Two of them shipped in private images before this line existed
# (dev/changelog/994).
channelbin-support-*.zip

# --- Recordings and scratch output ---
/dvr/
epg.xml
epg.txt

# --- Dev-only tree (docs, backlog, changelog, mockups, samples, screenshots) ---
dev/
# Source for the root of the Home Assistant integration's own public repo. It does not ship
# to the app's public repo, so a build context holding it fails the release-time check that
# refuses anything the public repo does not carry (dev/changelog/1089).
ha-integration/
# The integration itself stopped shipping to the app's public repo too (dev/changelog/1091),
# so the same check refuses a build context carrying it. Nothing in the image reads it: the
# integration runs inside Home Assistant, not inside this container.
custom_components/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
.claude/
.mcp.json
.playwright-mcp/
scripts/

# --- Repo docs, test and browser tooling: ship in the repo, have no job in a runtime image ---
# docs/ is the public repo's own documentation, including the README screenshots. README.md
# itself references those screenshots by relative path (docs/screenshots/*.png), so shipping
# the README without docs/ would leave seven broken images with nothing in the container ever
# reading it anyway - excluded rather than dragging docs/screenshots/ along just for this.
docs/
README.md
tests/
run_tests.sh
node_modules/
package.json
package-lock.json
playwright.config.ts

# --- Git, lint and editor ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gitignore.public
.publishignore
.flake8
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# --- Python build artifacts ---
# `**/` because a .dockerignore pattern is anchored at the context root: a bare
# `__pycache__/` only ever matched a root-level directory and let app/__pycache__ through.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Docker's own files (COPY . would otherwise put them in the image) ---
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.example.yml
# The Unraid Community Apps listing, read from the repository by the catalog's scanner.
ca_profile.xml
docker/unraid-template.xml
